# Sobelow configuration for Statifier-ex (st-21b).
#
# Read by `mix sobelow` and, in the quality gate, by ExQuality's Sobelow stage,
# which passes the parts of this file that say *what* to scan through to the
# tool and decides pass or fail itself against `exit:`.
#
# ADR-0011 guards this path: an edit here needs an entry in
# docs/quality-gate-changes.md. That is deliberate. The blocking threshold is a
# security decision, and a security decision should be a thing a human signs
# for when it moves.
#
# `exit: "low"` - every finding blocks, which is stricter than Sobelow's own
# default and than ExQuality's ("medium"). It has to be, here: Sobelow drops a
# Traversal, RCE or SQL finding to low confidence whenever the file it is in is
# not a Phoenix controller (see Sobelow.Traversal.FileModule), and Statifier is
# a library with no controllers at all. At "medium" those checks could never
# block anything and the scan would only be watching for hardcoded secrets,
# `binary_to_term`, and known-vulnerable deps. "low" is what makes the
# code-level checks real for a project shaped like this one.
#
# `ignore_files` excludes by path, with the reason stated, the way .credo.exs
# does - never by lowering a threshold to get past a finding:
#
#   lib/mix/statifier/gate_guard.ex, lib/mix/statifier/regression_registry.ex,
#   lib/mix/statifier/adr_guard.ex
#     Traversal.FileModule on File.read/1 and File.write/2. All three are Mix
#     task support modules: they run under `mix` on a developer's machine and
#     read paths that developer configured, so the path is not
#     attacker-controlled and never reaches the released library. Everything
#     under lib/statifier is scanned; only these three dev-only modules are
#     not, and a new one is not covered by this list until someone adds it
#     here.
#
# `skip: true` turns on Sobelow's inline `@sobelow_skip` annotation, which
# silences one named check on one function rather than excluding a whole file.
# It is here for st-m5c3's serialization contract: `:erlang.binary_to_term/2`
# is how a versioned blob is decoded, and Misc.BinToTerm fires on every call
# regardless of the `:safe` option. `ignore_files` is the wrong instrument for
# that - these are shipped library modules, not dev-only Mix support, and
# excluding one by path would take Traversal, RCE and the hardcoded-secret
# checks off it too. The inline form keeps every other check live and puts the
# silencing on the line it applies to, where a reviewer reads it.
#
# The cost, stated rather than discovered: an `@sobelow_skip` added anywhere
# under lib/ now takes effect with no edit to this file and so no ADR-0011
# entry. `grep -rn "@sobelow_skip" lib/` is the whole list; it is a diff-visible
# annotation on a named function, not a threshold, and every use of it owes the
# same in-code justification the two below carry.
[
  exit: "low",
  skip: true,
  ignore_files: [
    "lib/mix/statifier/gate_guard.ex",
    "lib/mix/statifier/regression_registry.ex",
    "lib/mix/statifier/adr_guard.ex"
  ]
]
